(7126738, 1088578, 108580, '<td valign="top">The need to shock in the modern day with reality TV, expansive Hollywood film productions,  privacy invasion newspapers and Paparazzi adds to the need for the unexpected, the different, the nipple piercing, and so on in modern stills work in order to stand out. I''d have enjoyed this just as much without the gas mask. Bold. 7. Very <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=100393" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Paul</a>-ish</td>', 'The need to shock in the modern day with reality TV, expansive Hollywood film productions,  privacy invasion newspapers and Paparazzi adds to the need for the unexpected, the different, the nipple piercing, and so on in modern stills work in order to stand out. I''d have enjoyed this just as much without the gas mask. Bold. 7. Very  Paul-ish', '2013-11-07 15:23:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(7126739, 1088423, 104230, '<td valign="top">Nice, slightly abstract, image. Back to bump.</td>', 'Nice, slightly abstract, image. Back to bump.', '2013-11-07 15:26:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(7126741, 1089050, 100393, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1051747" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100393/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1051747.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100393/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1051747.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100393/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1051747.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Awarded for the October 2013 Free Study, for the reasons identified below. <br/> <br/>This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is my only 10 - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. You''ve engaged me thoroughly - it normally takes some people in an image to do that for me, but here you''ve created something to stop me in my tracks and appreciate the quality.<br/> <br/>2. The quality of the post processing is stunning - so utterly well judged - so use of glow especially.<br/> <br/>3. The composition, brilliant enough for me to ignore the clipped top of the tree on the left. The perception of depth as we are drawn from the foreground fronds and reflections to the power of the waterfalls behind. This, coupled with the massive presence of the red mill - tremendous.<br/> <br/>4. The colours - the subtleness of most of the scene juxtaposed with the dramatically coloured mill works very well indeed.<br/> <br/>5. The low POV and how that accentuates a sense of depth.<br/> <br/>Overall, I can''t overlook the flat-out masterfulness of this image. Not my usual pickings but quality like this can''t be ignored. Looking forward to see who''s this is. I once saw a landscape of Sandy''s that left a similar impression but we''ll see...</td>', '  Awarded for the October 2013 Free Study, for the reasons identified below.  This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier)  Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is my only 10 - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. You''ve engaged me thoroughly - it normally takes some people in an image to do that for me, but here you''ve created something to stop me in my tracks and appreciate the quality. 2. The quality of the post processing is stunning - so utterly well judged - so use of glow especially. 3. The composition, brilliant enough for me to ignore the clipped top of the tree on the left. The perception of depth as we are drawn from the foreground fronds and reflections to the power of the waterfalls behind. This, coupled with the massive presence of the red mill - tremendous. 4. The colours - the subtleness of most of the scene juxtaposed with the dramatically coloured mill works very well indeed. 5. The low POV and how that accentuates a sense of depth. Overall, I can''t overlook the flat-out masterfulness of this image. Not my usual pickings but quality like this can''t be ignored. Looking forward to see who''s this is. I once saw a landscape of Sandy''s that left a similar impression but we''ll see...', '2013-11-07 15:28:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(7126742, 1089727, 104230, '<td valign="top">I like this pose, especially the tilt of his head.  Great light and B&amp;W processing. Back to comment and bump. Makes me want to stay and keep looking.</td>', 'I like this pose, especially the tilt of his head.  Great light and B&W processing. Back to comment and bump. Makes me want to stay and keep looking.', '2013-11-07 15:29:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(7126743, 1088592, 138630, '<td valign="top">Beautiful without the bird - perfect with it.  Lovely shimmery light and tones.  Top 10% for me.  Already voted, back to comment.</td>', 'Beautiful without the bird - perfect with it.  Lovely shimmery light and tones.  Top 10% for me.  Already voted, back to comment.', '2013-11-07 15:29:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(7126744, 1089715, 138630, '<td valign="top">My favorite of the ocean scenes, I think - I sure do love the water rushing in and the purples and pinks here.  Top 10% for me.  Already voted, back to comment.</td>', 'My favorite of the ocean scenes, I think - I sure do love the water rushing in and the purples and pinks here.  Top 10% for me.  Already voted, back to comment.', '2013-11-07 15:30:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(7126746, 1089837, 104230, '<td valign="top">Delightful, quirky and well captured and processed.  Back to comment and bump.</td>', 'Delightful, quirky and well captured and processed.  Back to comment and bump.', '2013-11-07 15:30:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(7126747, 1089838, 100393, '<td valign="top">This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is one of my 9s - I like it a lot. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. I always enjoy the use of blur, especially where is has ''structure'' - I see that here.<br/> <br/>2. Great title, I''d spotted the monopedal motif before I''d noticed your title, so the image communicates very well.<br/> <br/>3. Super toning - good choices here.<br/> <br/>4. The sense of dynamic flow.<br/> <br/>5. The foreground discarded cups - still and at odds with the runners.<br/> <br/>Overall, a most compelling image.</td>', 'This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier)  Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is one of my 9s - I like it a lot. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. I always enjoy the use of blur, especially where is has ''structure'' - I see that here. 2. Great title, I''d spotted the monopedal motif before I''d noticed your title, so the image communicates very well. 3. Super toning - good choices here. 4. The sense of dynamic flow. 5. The foreground discarded cups - still and at odds with the runners. Overall, a most compelling image.', '2013-11-07 15:32:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(7126748, 1087784, 104230, '<td valign="top">Well seen. Lovely colors, textures and composition. The posts and sign protruding from the wall provide a sense of depth that enhances the image. Back to comment and bump.</td>', 'Well seen. Lovely colors, textures and composition. The posts and sign protruding from the wall provide a sense of depth that enhances the image. Back to comment and bump.', '2013-11-07 15:33:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(7126751, 1089755, 100393, '<td valign="top">This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is one of my 9s - I like it a lot. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: <br/> <br/>1. The figure of the girl adds such mystery; from this POV I feel hidden, furtive, like we are on her tail - she''s under surveillance.<br/> <br/>2. I love the position of the sun and the cascading flare.<br/> <br/>3. I really like how you''ve managed the contrast - giving us more dynamic range and shunning the temptation to silhouette the tree..<br/> <br/>Overall, this image is transportive and effective. I like it a lot.</td>', 'This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier)  Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is one of my 9s - I like it a lot. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:  1. The figure of the girl adds such mystery; from this POV I feel hidden, furtive, like we are on her tail - she''s under surveillance. 2. I love the position of the sun and the cascading flare. 3. I really like how you''ve managed the contrast - giving us more dynamic range and shunning the temptation to silhouette the tree.. Overall, this image is transportive and effective. I like it a lot.', '2013-11-07 15:40:30.000000', NULL, 1),
