(7126755, 1088923, 104230, '<td valign="top">Lovely delicate capture of these dead hydrangea flowers.  I find myself wishing that the depth of field extended a bit further so as to include the texture on the back of first set of petals that are just out of focus, rather than as it is which seems to be mainly on the edges of the front petals.</td>', 'Lovely delicate capture of these dead hydrangea flowers.  I find myself wishing that the depth of field extended a bit further so as to include the texture on the back of first set of petals that are just out of focus, rather than as it is which seems to be mainly on the edges of the front petals.', '2013-11-07 15:47:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(7126757, 1088167, 104230, '<td valign="top">Lovely! Great capture of the light and textures. Back to comment and bump.</td>', 'Lovely! Great capture of the light and textures. Back to comment and bump.', '2013-11-07 15:48:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(7126760, 1086443, 100393, '<td valign="top">This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is one of my 8s - I like it. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. Great low fidelity image - lovely well matched tone and grain.<br/> <br/>2. I love the iconic M being juxtaposed with the steeple - it provokes thinking around capitalist and religious doctrine and the social gullibility that is endemic within our world.<br/> <br/>3. I love that pole on the left - random and stark, a distractor for distraction''s sake.<br/> <br/>Overall, a nicely made (counterculture) image.</td>', 'This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier)  Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is one of my 8s - I like it. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. Great low fidelity image - lovely well matched tone and grain. 2. I love the iconic M being juxtaposed with the steeple - it provokes thinking around capitalist and religious doctrine and the social gullibility that is endemic within our world. 3. I love that pole on the left - random and stark, a distractor for distraction''s sake. Overall, a nicely made (counterculture) image.', '2013-11-07 16:00:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(7126762, 1089737, 100393, '<td valign="top">This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is one of my 8s - I like it. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: <br/> <br/>1. I like unusual portraits and this is no difference - you''ve made eclectic choices here that I admire:<br/> <br/>2. Your young but old (fashioned subject).<br/> <br/>3. Your ''patchy'' processing with subtle blur and smoothed textures.<br/> <br/>4. Your willing to preserve the shadows in the eye sockets.<br/> <br/>5. The gap above the tie.<br/> <br/>6. The competing window.<br/> <br/>7. The posed but candid feel.<br/> <br/>Very nicely made.</td>', 'This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier)  Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is one of my 8s - I like it. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:  1. I like unusual portraits and this is no difference - you''ve made eclectic choices here that I admire: 2. Your young but old (fashioned subject). 3. Your ''patchy'' processing with subtle blur and smoothed textures. 4. Your willing to preserve the shadows in the eye sockets. 5. The gap above the tie. 6. The competing window. 7. The posed but candid feel. Very nicely made.', '2013-11-07 16:03:38.000000', NULL, 1),
